{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787357220465001881,"compiled_state":{"alias":"bold-abeyant-indri","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"e084222d65cb2a8d028f4399628c10f60d272334d546202a25851b711fce0065","event_uuid":"78611ccc-e1fb-4861-b05b-644d4339a680","position":{"commit_sha":"2bef5b27eecee2e574dd8184ef56b85d1b7711ad","position":"1787354731920556001-78611ccc-e1fb-4861-b05b-644d4339a680"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d324f063403e29fd449ca618ad32728357eafd02de6c1dc82cfbb9ebea00cc03","event_uuid":"a1b9f14a-c92f-46cc-b38b-0a9f86aab49f","position":{"commit_sha":"86fcd0a71b9424e1d839d65a9a08c8ef1545a8bf","position":"1787354738508094001-a1b9f14a-c92f-46cc-b38b-0a9f86aab49f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9907d78ffafb2bd392e95efc4705e725e9dfed480bf5458f782d5f00578a3b12","event_uuid":"48576720-1a28-40ce-ae8d-9c09c56ab40f","position":{"commit_sha":"c9d90ff7796986d5ef193c44224b7e3025eef86b","position":"1787354745552118001-48576720-1a28-40ce-ae8d-9c09c56ab40f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787354731920556001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"48576720-1a28-40ce-ae8d-9c09c56ab40f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2d9a-78c5-5f87-4a22"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nTwenty-seven bugs in the fortnight defect review were tests that could not fail or that burned CI time: subprocess oracles asserting only that a string is absent with no return-code check (`obvious-saline-gerbil`, `sound-bumpkinly-thrush`), a test burning the full 120 s Jira readiness budget per xdist worker (`albinic-kyanite-goldeneye`), wall-clock oracles (`tapestried-abhorrent-tuna`). The project already runs `scripts/check_wall_clock_asserts.py` and pins `pytest-timeout==2.4.0`, but the budget is set only on the CI command line (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:656-672`, `--timeout=300`), so local runs have none, and Ruff does not select `PLW1510` (subprocess.run without `check=`) or the `PT` flake8-pytest-style family. Operator decision (2026-08-21): adopt only what is common practice in maintained OSS projects; a 20-second per-test budget is approved with an explicit override for tests that must be slow.\n\n## Approach\nStandard tooling only, no custom linter: (1) add `PLW1510` and `PT` to `[tool.ruff.lint] select` in `pyproject.toml`, clearing the existing backlog in the same change (PT findings that are stylistic go in `ignore` with a comment, not per-line `noqa`); (2) move the per-test budget into `[tool.pytest.ini_options]`: `timeout = 20`, `timeout_method = \"thread\"`, `timeout_func_only = true`, and drop `--timeout=300` from the CI invocation so the ini value applies; (3) the override is `@pytest.mark.timeout(N, func_only=True)` on tests that must be slow, each carrying a one-line comment naming why; (4) add `check_wall_clock_asserts.py` and `check_raw_git_writes.py` to `make lint` (the pattern task `aciduric-enhanced-piranha` establishes). Not adopted because no maintained tool does it: lints for subprocess `timeout=`, `sleep` budgets, `os.environ.copy()`, `sys.modules` writes, foreign `.git/` writes; the `xdist_group` case is already covered by `tests/unit/test_live_jira_xdist_confinement.py`.\n\n## Scope\n`pyproject.toml`, `Makefile`, `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`, `tests/**` (backlog fixes for PLW1510/PT and `timeout` marks on slow tests), `docs/local-dev-env.md` (document the override).\n\n## Testing\nMechanical plus one behavioural check: a deliberately sleeping 25 s test fails under the ini budget and passes with the marker. Pinning: the full default tier passes under `-n 4` with the new budget; `make lint` is green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `ruff check` with `PLW1510` and `PT` selected reports zero findings on `main`; checked by `make lint`.\n- [ ] A test exceeding 20 s without the marker fails locally and in CI; a marked test passes; checked by the two-test probe (removed before landing or kept under `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py` with the slow one marked).\n- [ ] `make lint` runs the wall-clock and raw-git checks; checked by `make -n lint`.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"approved remediation edit"},{"path":"Makefile","reason":"approved remediation edit"},{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"approved remediation edit"},{"path":"docs/local-dev-env.md","reason":"approved remediation edit"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py","reason":"approved remediation edit"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a"],["relates_to","2d9a-78c5-5f87-4a22"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["gates","fortnight-review"],"ticket_id":"73b8-2d79-3046-44ce","ticket_type":"story","title":"Adopt standard test-hygiene tooling: ruff PLW1510 + PT, pytest-timeout 20 s budget with marker override, hygiene checks in make lint","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["78611ccc-e1fb-4861-b05b-644d4339a680","a1b9f14a-c92f-46cc-b38b-0a9f86aab49f","48576720-1a28-40ce-ae8d-9c09c56ab40f"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787357220465001881,"uuid":"97c5cf5e-d4c2-4e75-8b96-b81cca448976"}